  "question": {
    "text": "A saturated solution of $\\mathrm{BaSO}_{4}$ at $25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ is $4 \\times 10^{-5} \\mathrm{M}$. The solubility of $\\mathrm{BaSO}_{4}$ in $0.1 \\mathrm{M} \\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{SO}_{4}$ at this temperature will be"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$1.6 \\times 10^{-9} \\mathrm{M}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$1.6 \\times 10^{-8} \\mathrm{M}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$4 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{M}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$4 \\times 10^{-4} \\mathrm{M}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{array}{r}\r\n\\mathrm{BaSO}_{4} \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{Ba}^{2+}+\\mathrm{SO}_{4}^{2-} \\\\\r\n\\mathrm{s} \\quad \\mathrm{s}+0.1 \\\\\r\n\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{SO}_{4} \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{Na}^{+}+\\mathrm{SO}_{4}^{2-} \\\\\r\n0.2 \\quad 0.1\r\n\\end{array}$\r\n$\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{sp}}=\\left[\\mathrm{Ba}^{+2}\\right]\\left[\\mathrm{SO}_{4}^{-2}\\right] \\\\\r\n\\therefore 4 \\times 10^{-5}=\\mathrm{s} \\times(\\mathrm{s}+0.1)\r\n\\end{array}$\r\nor $4 \\times 10^{-5} \\approx \\mathrm{s} \\times 0.1 \\quad \\therefore \\mathrm{s}=4 \\times 10^{-4}$ as $\\mathrm{s}<< < 0.1 \\quad \\therefore \\mathrm{s}+0.1 \\approx 0.1$"
  }
}